In this case, since you're using `setTimeout`, it's essentially creating a timer for each iteration of your loop. Since there's only one instance of the `var` declaration, every time you call `setTimeout` on the same variable, it creates a new instance of the variable, which then prints the same number five times.

To fix this issue, you can either change your `var` declarations inside functions or use a different approach like using `let` instead of `var`. However, if you want to avoid changing your `var` declarations, you could consider using `const` instead of `var`, but keep in mind that `const` also has its own limitations.

